They are some built functions that commonly used : print(), len(), str(), list(), tuple(), dir(), dict(), int(), float(), min(), max(), sum(), type(), sorted(), open(), file(), help(), and input().
Output and Input:----
print(): Displays text or variables to the screen.
input(): Prompts the user for text input from the keyboard.

Data Inspection:----
type(): Returns the data type of an object.
dir(): Lists all properties and methods of an object.
help(): Invokes the built-in help system for documentation.

Type Conversion (Casting):----
str(): Converts a value into a string data type.
int(): Converts a value into an integer whole number.
float(): Converts a value into a decimal number.
list(): Converts an iterable collection into a mutable list.
tuple(): Converts an iterable collection into an immutable tuple.
dict(): Creates a dictionary collection of key-value pairs.

Math and Collections:----
len(): Returns the number of items in a collection.
sum(): Adds up all numerical items in a collection.
min(): Finds the smallest value in a collection.
max(): Finds the largest value in a collection.
sorted(): Returns a new sorted list from a collection.

File Handling:----
open(): Opens a file for reading, writing, or appending.
file(): Obsolete function from Python 2; no longer exists.


